(*  Interpretation: the transverse fields are not dephasing fields on the probes. ZZ probes still have a Schur channel and rank at most four; Exchange need not be unital or U(1)-covariant. Covariance plots measure deviations and are not symmetry constraints asserted by this workflow. Choi negativity refers to reference-versus-output entanglement, not entanglement between A and B. The plotted State Concurrence is edge-edge entanglement. The ZZ EntanglingConcurrence is the exact maximum over separable edge inputs for this fixed bulk, not an optimization over bulk states. No infinite-time average is computed.  *)


